<article class="env-lemma" id="04ZD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04ZD">Lemma <span data-tag="04ZD">29.9.6</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ f \ar[rd]_ p &  &  Y \ar[dl]^ q \\  &  Z }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes. If $f$ is surjective and $p$ is quasi-compact, then $q$ is quasi-compact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $W \subset Z$ be a quasi-compact open. By assumption $p^{-1}(W)$ is quasi-compact. Hence by Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/04Z9" data-tag="04Z9">5.12.7</a> the inverse image $q^{-1}(W) = f(p^{-1}(W))$ is quasi-compact too. This proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>